('74e87764-7f3f-55fc-990e-5668c74f9bb5'::uuid, 'SP Resolution No. 2023-347: authority to sign the MOA with CPR-RIMT Rapid Rescue Rider Ormoc Chapter', 'city_issuance', null, 'SP Res. No. 2023-347', 'Sangguniang Panlungsod', '2023-12-29'::date, 'Accredited CSO provides CDRRMO-accredited volunteers to augment HEMS and the CDRRMO; the City trains and supplies them and is accountable for volunteer injury or loss. The annexed MOA copy is unsigned.', array['A2.7','A2.8','A10.2','B6.1']::text[], 'https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MGgm_n5Od7S6W7JFy_u9IWf2J37JQbb9/view', 'Project Drive (CDRRMO folder); scanned copy, text read by OCR', 'current', 'standard', array[]::public.app_role[]),
('2560647d-9bd1-57fd-a465-86405387302b'::uuid, 'Amending Section 6 of Ordinance No. 135, s. 2023 (Policy on suspending or cancelling classes and work during emergencies or disasters)', 'city_issuance', null, 'SP Ordinance No. 189, s. 2025', 'Sangguniang Panlungsod', '2025-04-08'::date, 'Enacted 8 Apr 2025 (145th regular session); approved by Mayor Lucy Torres-Gomez. Tertiary in-person classes are suspended when PAGASA issues a Red Rainfall Warning AND there is actual heavy rainfall in Ormoc; with a Red warning but no heavy rain, the school head may keep classes after consulting the official platform the CDRRMO provides for the local situation. Online, hybrid or asynchronous classes may continue during a suspension. The City Mayor decides when there is flooding under an Orange, Yellow or no rainfall warning. New duties: the CDRRMO holds coordination meetings with all school DRRM coordinators on school disaster and contingency plans and trains the education sector; the CDRRMC requires schools to record in enrolment forms which students live in flood-prone and other risk areas. Joint committee minutes of 2 Apr 2025 attached (CDRRMO represented).', array['A1.5','A6.2','A7.1','A7.7','C4.2']::text[], 'https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TBDjosHkhf0QOpifePnffwfid8jO0Hso/view', null, 'current', 'standard', array[]::public.app_role[]),
